.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH author 1  "author " 
.SH NAME
author \- Porcelain: Declaratively compile and stage a JSON batch of authoring claims
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBauthor\fR [\fB\-e\fR|\fB\-\-example\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fICLAIMS_FILE\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Porcelain: Declaratively compile and stage a JSON batch of authoring claims
.PP
Accepts a JSON array of AuthorClaim objects via FILE or stdin (\-).
.PP
Example JSON claims input: [ { "kind": "create_element", "type_id": "kat.core/requirement", "title": "Auth Requirement", "handle": "@req\-auth" }, { "kind": "create_element", "type_id": "kat.core/implementation", "title": "Auth Module", "handle": "@imp\-auth" }, { "kind": "link_element", "relationship_type_id": "kat.core/realizes", "source_ref": "@imp\-auth", "target_ref": "@req\-auth" } ]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-example\fR
Print a working JSON authoring claim template example
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output structured machine JSON envelope
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fICLAIMS_FILE\fR]
Path to JSON file containing declarative claims (reads stdin if omitted or \*(Aq\-\*(Aq)
